{"id": "gpt-money-19", "category": "money", "difficulty": "hard", "description": "Acceptance criteria: - A cash batch is exactly three canonical positive amounts from 1 through 99, separated by commas. No two amounts may have identical decimal spellings. No currency symbol or spaces. - Evaluate the input as supplied; do not trim or normalize it.", "regex": "/^([1-9][0-9]?),(?!\\1,)([1-9][0-9]?),(?!\\1$)(?!\\2$)[1-9][0-9]?$(?![\\s\\S])/", "tests": {"match": ["1,2,3", "99,98,97", "1,10,99", "10,1,20", "5,50,55", "12,34,56", "90,9,19", "2,22,23"], "no_match": ["1,1,2", "1,2,1", "1,2,2", "0,1,2", "100,1,2", "01,2,3", "1, 2,3", "!1,2,3", "1,2,3!", "1,2,3\n", "1,2,3\r", "1,2,3\r\n", "1,2,3 ", "1,2,3 ", " 1,2,3", "1,2,3 "]}}
{"id": "gpt-multiline-16", "category": "multiline", "difficulty": "hard", "description": "A localized two-line label: the literal prefix title= followed by 2 through 12 Unicode letter clusters. Each cluster is a Unicode letter followed by zero to two Unicode combining marks. One optional ASCII hyphen may join two nonempty runs of clusters, but no edge hyphen or second hyphen is allowed. Length counts letter clusters, excluding the hyphen and any fixed prefix; spaces, digits and other characters are forbidden. No normalization is performed. Append the exact literal suffix LF followed by status=ok after the name; its characters do not count toward the cluster limit.", "regex": "/^title=(?=(?:\\p{L}\\p{M}{0,2}-?){2,12}\\nstatus=ok$)(?:\\p{L}\\p{M}{0,2}){1,12}(?:-(?:\\p{L}\\p{M}{0,2}){1,12})?\\nstatus=ok$(?![\\s\\S])/u", "tests": {"match": ["title=ab\nstatus=ok", "title=éx\nstatus=ok", "title=á̈b\nstatus=ok", "title=東京-大阪\nstatus=ok", "title=Δέλτα\nstatus=ok", "title=مرحبا\nstatus=ok", "title=Зима\nstatus=ok", "title=abcdefghijkl\nstatus=ok", "title=é-ë\nstatus=ok", "title=Aé\nstatus=ok"], "no_match": ["title=a\nstatus=ok", "title=abcdefghijklm\nstatus=ok", "title=ab1\nstatus=ok", "title=a_b\nstatus=ok", "title=a b\nstatus=ok", "title=é\nstatus=ok", "title=😀a\nstatus=ok", "title=́ab\nstatus=ok", "title=á̈̃b\nstatus=ok", "title=-ab\nstatus=ok", "title=ab-\nstatus=ok", "title=a--b\nstatus=ok", "title=ab-cd-ef\nstatus=ok", "title=ab", "title=ab?status=ok", "title=ab\nSTATUS=OK", "!title=ab\nstatus=ok", "title=ab\nstatus=ok!", "title=ab\nstatus=ok\n", "title=ab\nstatus=ok\r", "title=ab\nstatus=ok\r\n", "title=ab\nstatus=ok ", "title=ab\nstatus=ok ", " title=ab\nstatus=ok", "title=ab\nstatus=ok "]}}
{"id": "gpt-multiline-20", "category": "multiline", "difficulty": "hard", "description": "A balanced text block uses LF only. First line is a lowercase ASCII label 3 to 8 letters in matching single or double quotes, second line is exactly four ASCII digits, and third line repeats the exact quote-label-quote first line. Label must not be end; no final LF.", "regex": "/^(['\\\"])(?!end\\1)([a-z]{3,8})\\1\\n[0-9]{4}\\n\\1\\2\\1$(?![\\s\\S])/", "tests": {"match": ["'abc'\n0000\n'abc'", "\"xyz\"\n9999\n\"xyz\"", "'abcdefgh'\n1234\n'abcdefgh'", "'data'\n1000\n'data'", "\"word\"\n0001\n\"word\"", "\"title\"\n9876\n\"title\""], "no_match": ["'end'\n1234\n'end'", "'abc'\n1234\n'xyz'", "'abc'\n1234\n\"abc\"", "'abc\"\n1234\n'abc'", "'ab'\n1234\n'ab'", "'abc'\n123\n'abc'", "'abc'\r\n1234\n'abc'", "!'abc'\n0000\n'abc'", "'abc'\n0000\n'abc'!", "'abc'\n0000\n'abc'\n", "'abc'\n0000\n'abc'\r", "'abc'\n0000\n'abc'\r\n", "'abc'\n0000\n'abc' ", "'abc'\n0000\n'abc' ", " 'abc'\n0000\n'abc'", "'abc'\n0000\n'abc' ", "?abc?\n1234\n?abc?", "'ab!'\n1234\n'ab!'", "'abc'\n12a4\n'abc'"]}, "examples": {"match": ["'sample'\n5555\n'sample'", "\"ends\"\n4321\n\"ends\""], "no_match": []}}
{"id": "gpt-network-17", "category": "network", "difficulty": "hard", "description": "A packet note: the entire string has the literal opening wrapper NET{, a lowercase ASCII routing label of 2 through 6 letters, colon, a body, colon, the exact same routing label and the literal closing wrapper }NET. The body has 1 through 40 Unicode code points, allows any characters including line breaks and colons, and must contain the lowercase substring packet. Only the body counts toward its length limit; no other text is allowed.", "regex": "/^NET\\{(?<route>[a-z]{2,6}):(?=.{1,40}:\\k<route>\\}NET$)(?=.{0,40}packet.{0,40}:\\k<route>\\}NET$).*:\\k<route>\\}NET$(?![\\s\\S])/su", "tests": {"match": ["NET{aa:packet:aa}NET", "NET{abcdef:apacket:abcdef}NET", "NET{route:\npacket:route}NET", "NET{memo:packet\n:memo}NET", "NET{zz:😀packet:zz}NET", "NET{key:xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxpacket:key}NET", "NET{xy:😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀packet:xy}NET", "NET{aa:prefix: packet: suffix:aa}NET"], "no_match": ["NET{aa::aa}NET", "NET{aa:abc:aa}NET", "NET{aa:xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxpacket:aa}NET", "NET{aa:packet:ab}NET", "NET{a:packet:a}NET", "NET{abcdefg:packet:abcdefg}NET", "NET{AA:packet:AA}NET", "NET{aa:PACKET:aa}NET", "NET{aa:packet:aa", "aa:packet:aa}NET", "NET{aa:😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀packet:aa}NET", "NET{packet:abc:packet}NET", "NET{aa:packet:aa}NET!", "NET{aa:packet:aa}NET\n", "NET{aa:packet:aa}NET\r", "NET{aa:packet:aa}NET\r\n", "NET{aa:packet:aa}NET ", "NET{aa:packet:aa}NET ", " NET{aa:packet:aa}NET", "NET{aa:packet:aa}NET "]}, "examples": {"match": ["NET{tag:packetb:tag}NET", "NET{ab:\tpacket:ab}NET"], "no_match": ["!NET{aa:packet:aa}NET"]}}
